-- je54-art07-service-by-post: Article 7 of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, "Meaning of service by post", for a given TEXT of the Law.
-- Article 7 was the original Article 12 (Table of Renumbered Provisions); it is the same in all seven deposited texts; a question about service before 1 January 2019 refuses (no text of those years is deposited).
-- Selecting date: the day the letter was posted (the day the fact occurred).
--
-- What the Article says.  Where an enactment authorizes or requires any document to be served by post, whatever word it uses, then unless the contrary intention appears (1) service is deemed effected by properly
-- addressing, prepaying and posting a letter containing the document, and (2) unless the contrary is proved, it is deemed effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
-- (2) is a presumption about the TIME, rebuttable.  It is neither the day of posting nor the day of actual receipt as such.  It does not apply to any other mode of service.  The Law does not say how long post takes.

§ `Article 7: Meaning of service by post`

-- src:27 | Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, authorizes or requires any document to be served by post, whether the expression “serve”, “give” or “send”, or any other expression is used, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the service shall be deemed to be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting a letter containing the document, and, unless the contrary is proved, to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 7 (src:27)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 7 deals only with a document to be served by post` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 7 deals only where an enactment authorizes or requires a document to be served by post; it says nothing of any other mode of service"

-- src:27 | Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, authorizes or requires any document to be served by post, whether the expression “serve”, “give” or “send”, or any other expression is used, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the service shall be deemed to be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting a letter containing the document, and, unless the contrary is proved, to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 7 (src:27)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 7: a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 7 does not say when or whether service by post is then deemed effected"

-- src:27 | Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, authorizes or requires any document to be served by post, whether the expression “serve”, “give” or “send”, or any other expression is used, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the service shall be deemed to be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting a letter containing the document, and, unless the contrary is proved, to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 7 (src:27)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 7: service is not deemed effected, so there is no time` MEANS
    REFUSE "service by post is not deemed effected under Article 7 (the letter was not properly addressed, prepaid and posted), so the Article gives no time"

-- src:27 | Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, authorizes or requires any document to be served by post, whether the expression “serve”, “give” or “send”, or any other expression is used, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the service shall be deemed to be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting a letter containing the document, and, unless the contrary is proved, to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 7 (src:27)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 7: the contrary is proved and the Article gives no time` MEANS
    REFUSE "the contrary is proved: on the reading that Article 7 says nothing of the time once the presumption is rebutted, the Article gives no time"

-- (1) "service shall be deemed to be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting a letter containing the document".  If the letter was not properly addressed, prepaid and posted, Article 7 does not
-- deem service effected; it does not say that service was not effected.
-- src:27 | Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, authorizes or requires any document to be served by post, whether the expression “serve”, “give” or “send”, or any other expression is used, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the service shall be deemed to be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting a letter containing the document, and, unless the contrary is proved, to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 7 (src:27)
GIVEN s IS A `Service by post as it happened`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the letter was properly addressed, prepaid and posted` s MEANS
        s's `the letter was properly addressed`
    AND s's `the letter was prepaid`
    AND s's `the letter was posted`

-- src:27 | Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, authorizes or requires any document to be served by post, whether the expression “serve”, “give” or “send”, or any other expression is used, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the service shall be deemed to be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting a letter containing the document, and, unless the contrary is proved, to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 7 (src:27)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      s IS A `Service by post as it happened`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 7: service by post is deemed effected` v s `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT s's `the enactment authorizes or requires the document to be served by post` THEN `Article 7 deals only with a document to be served by post`
           IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 7: a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide`
           OTHERWISE `the letter was properly addressed, prepaid and posted` s

-- (2) "unless the contrary is proved, to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post".  Fork I4: once the contrary is proved, the time that is proved governs (taken:
-- the presumption is about the time at which service was effected, and what rebuts it is proof of the time at which it was in fact effected); on the other reading the Article is silent and gives no time.
-- src:27 | Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, authorizes or requires any document to be served by post, whether the expression “serve”, “give” or “send”, or any other expression is used, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the service shall be deemed to be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting a letter containing the document, and, unless the contrary is proved, to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 7 (src:27)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      s IS A `Service by post as it happened`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      reading IS A `What governs once the presumption of Article 7 is rebutted` TYPICALLY `the time that is proved`
GIVETH A `Local moment`
`Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` v s `a contrary intention appears` reading MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `Article 7: service by post is deemed effected` v s `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 7: service is not deemed effected, so there is no time`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER s's `the other time proved`
               WHEN NOTHING THEN s's `the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`
               WHEN JUST proved THEN
                   CONSIDER reading
                   WHEN `the time that is proved` THEN proved
                   WHEN `the Article gives no time` THEN `Article 7: the contrary is proved and the Article gives no time`

-- src:27 | Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, authorizes or requires any document to be served by post, whether the expression “serve”, “give” or “send”, or any other expression is used, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the service shall be deemed to be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting a letter containing the document, and, unless the contrary is proved, to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 7 (src:27)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      s IS A `Service by post as it happened`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      reading IS A `What governs once the presumption of Article 7 is rebutted` TYPICALLY `the time that is proved`
GIVETH A DATE
`Article 7: the day on which service by post is deemed effected` v s `a contrary intention appears` reading MEANS
    (`Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` v s `a contrary intention appears` reading)'s `calendar day`
